ecting it to other endangered incumbents, a sign the party sees the seat slipping away.\n\nTom Kean Jr. still holds real advantages: he has raised slightly more than Bennett and enters the final stretch with $3.6 million on hand, and he retains local endorsements including a major union. But a monthslong absence from Congress, a depression diagnosis, and healthcare-focused attacks have defined the closing weeks. Bennett's outside-spending edge and high-profile surrogates add pressure. The district's even partisanship keeps a path open, but the evidence favors Bennett.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.8072, "margin": 5.29}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.8017, "margin": 5.2}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.8142, "margin": 5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8286, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.794, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.7844, "margin": 5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.8491, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.8475, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.8242, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.8701, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.8531, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.8673, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.8347, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.7967, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.7946, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.7917, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.8497, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.8389, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.8307, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.8316, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.8538, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-13", "p_dem": 0.8638, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-14", "p_dem": 0.8747, "margin": 7.4}]}